menu "Leap low settings"

    config LEAP_DEFAULT_STA_SSID
        string "Fallback Wi-Fi SSID when no credentials are saved"
        default "Maturo"
        help
            Used only before provisioning. Saved credentials from the
            provisioning page always take precedence.

    config LEAP_DEFAULT_STA_PASSWORD
        string "Fallback Wi-Fi password when no credentials are saved"
        default "maturo2026"

    config LEAP_HEADING_HOLD
        bool "Hold IMU heading while driving straight"
        default y
        help
            When a straight velocity command (angular.z == 0) starts, latch the
            IMU heading and trim the left/right wheel targets with a PI loop to
            keep it. Corrects drift that encoder-only wheel sync cannot see
            (wheel diameter mismatch, slip, residual speed error). Disable only
            for A/B comparison.

    config MICRO_ROS_LOCAL_PORT
        string "micro-ROS local UDP port"
        default "8888"

    config MICROROS_TELEMETRY_BEST_EFFORT
        bool "Use best-effort reliability for odom, motor debug and scan (A/B test)"
        default n
        help
            Diagnostic A/B switch. Only changes the reliability policy of
            /odom, /motor_debug and /scan publishers; all other QoS settings,
            subscriptions and services remain unchanged. Best-effort publishers
            cannot deliver to reliable-only subscriptions.

    config MICROROS_DISABLE_SCAN_AB_TEST
        bool "Disable LaserScan publication (network A/B test only)"
        default n
        help
            Keep the /scan publisher entity but skip its periodic rcl_publish
            call. This isolates the bandwidth and IP-fragmentation effect of
            LaserScan without changing motor control, /cmd_vel, other topic
            rates, or their QoS. Do not use this diagnostic build for normal
            navigation because /scan will have no samples.

    config MICROROS_SCAN_POINT_COUNT
        int "Published LaserScan point count"
        range 90 360
        default 320
        help
            Downsample the lidar's 360 one-degree bins to this many published
            bins, retaining the closest valid return in each angular bin. 320
            points serialize to about 1344 bytes, keeping the resulting XRCE
            UDP datagram below a 1500-byte WLAN IP MTU. Using 360 points
            serializes to about 1504 bytes before XRCE/UDP/IP overhead and can
            trigger IP fragmentation on phone hotspots.

endmenu
